### Unpivot
Converts wide tables (one column per category) into tall tables (one row per value). One of the most important transformations for making real-world data usable in Power BI.

**Example — before:**

| Product | Jan | Feb | Mar |
|---|---|---|---|
| Widget A | 100 | 120 | 90 |

**After unpivot:**

| Product | Month | Sales |
|---|---|---|
| Widget A | Jan | 100 |
| Widget A | Feb | 120 |
| Widget A | Mar | 90 |

**How:**
Select the columns you want to keep fixed → right-click the remaining columns → Unpivot Other Columns

**In M code:**
```m
= Table.UnpivotOtherColumns(Source, {"Product"}, "Month", "Sales")
```

> 📸 Screenshot: Wide table → select fixed columns → Unpivot Other Columns → tall result
